  73: 
  74:     Rule:
  75:     - Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.
  76:     - A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.
  77:     - If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).
  78:     - If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).
  79: 
  80:     Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.
