 124:     - The right zone is empty black space above a grey baseline on the last row.
 125: 
 126:     Rule:
 127:     - Group left-zone cells by color and recover the two same-color anti-diagonal segments for each group.
 128:     - For every main-diagonal axis covered by both segments of a pair, fill the black cells strictly between the two segments with red.
 129:     - Count the filled red cells for each pair as its area, sort the pairs by increasing area, and draw one-cell-wide bars in the right zone on odd columns above the grey baseline using the pair's original color and area as height.
 130:     - Keep the original segments, the red fill, and the baseline.
 131: 
 132:     Key insight:
 133:     - The same diagonal fill serves two roles at once: it is the visible left-side transformation and also the quantitative measurement that controls right-side bar ordering and heights.
 134:     """
